<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yang Yinglong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1551–1600</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yang Yinglong was the last hereditary chief of Bozhou, a native chiefdom in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guizhou">Guizhou</a> ruled by the Yang family for some seven centuries. He rebelled against the Ming in 1589, a revolt counted among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wanli-emperor">Wanli Emperor</a>'s Three Great Campaigns. In 1600 a large Ming army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-hualong">Li Hualong</a> stormed his fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hailongtun">Hailongtun</a> and he killed himself; Bozhou was then placed under direct administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yang-yinglong.jpg" alt="Yang Yinglong" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alphaarea · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B5%B7%E9%BE%99%E5%B1%AF_%E5%9F%8E%E5%A2%99.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
